# Each standard cell the netlist uses, its Verilog model as gate.ys reads it against the
# function the Liberty file gives it, the file the flow synthesised against: two views of
# the cell from different sources, which have to agree for the gate model to mean the
# chip. The Makefile appends one block per cell after these lines. equiv_simple steps a
# flop without looking at which clock edge moves it, so the Liberty flops are asserted
# to take the rising edge there and the model's in gate.ys.

read_liberty -ignore_miss_func cells.lib
design -stash liberty

read_verilog ../netlist_equiv/primitives.v cells.v
hierarchy
proc
flatten
design -stash model
